// 004.12, 007.6 (T21, #80): a normative conflict on `c` taints intermediate derived facts
// reading `c` positively or negatively, so dependent act/power guards become `undetermined`
// (while two-valued saturation and explicit assignments `004.3` remain intact).
Fact p Identified by A.
Bool x.

Fact c Identified by p
  Default yes-rule Holds when x()
  Default no-rule Rejects when x().

Fact d-neg Identified by p Holds when Not(c(p)).
Fact d-chain Identified by p Holds when d-neg(p).

Power act-on-chain Actor p
  Holds when d-chain(p)
  Valid when d-chain(p).

Scenario transitive-conflict-makes-guard-undetermined {
  +x().
  ?Conflict(c(A)).
  ?d-neg(A).
  ?d-chain(A).
  ?undetermined act-on-chain(A).
  ?!valid act-on-chain(A).
  ?!lawful act-on-chain(A).
}

Scenario explicit-assignment-beats-taint {
  +x().
  +d-chain(A).
  ?Conflict(c(A)).
  ?valid act-on-chain(A).
  ?lawful act-on-chain(A).
}

Scenario priority-clears-transitive-taint {
  +x().
  Extend Fact c Priority no-rule Over yes-rule.
  ?!Conflict(c(A)).
  ?d-chain(A).
  ?valid act-on-chain(A).
  ?lawful act-on-chain(A).
}
